{title: Come, O Thou Traveler Unknown}
{key: C}
{time: 3/4}

{start_of_verse: 1}
Come, [C]O Thou [G]Trave[Em]ler un[Dm]known, whom [C]still I [F]hold but [G]cannot [Dm]see
My [C]compa[G]ny be[Em]fore is [Dm]gone, and [C]I am [Dm]left a[G]lone with [C]Thee
With [C]Thee all [G]night I [Em]mean to [G]stay, and [C]wrestle [Em]till the b[Dm]reak of d[G]ay
With [C]Thee all [G]night I [Em]mean to [G]stay, and [C]wrestle [Dm]till the [G]break of [C]day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
I [C]need not [G]tell Thee [Em]who I [Dm]am, my [C]sin and [F]mise[G]ry de[Dm]clare
Thy[C]self hast [G]called me [Em]by my [Dm]name, look [C]on Thy [Dm]hands, & [G]read it [C]there
But [C]who, I [G]ask Thee, [Em]who art [G]Thou? Tell [C]me Thy [Em]name, and [Dm]tell me [G]now
But [C]who, I [G]ask Thee, [Em]who art [G]Thou? Tell [C]me Thy [Dm]name, and [G]tell me [C]now.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Yield [C]to me [G]now, for [Em]I am [Dm]weak, but [C]confi[F]dent in [G]selfdes[Dm]pair
Speak [C]to my [G]heart, in [Em]blessings [Dm]speak, be [C]conquered [Dm]by my [G]instant [C]prayer
Speak, [C]or Thou [G]never [Em]hence shalt [G]move, and [C]tell me [Em]if Thy [Dm]name be [G]Love
Speak, [C]or Thou [G]never [Em]hence shalt [G]move, and [C]tell me [Dm]if Thy [G]name be [C]Love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Tis [C]Love! Tis [G]Love! Thou [Em]diedst for [Dm]me, I [C]hear Thy [F]whisper [G]in my [Dm]heart
The [C]morning [G]breaks, the [Em]shadows [Dm]flee: pure, [C]uni[Dm]versal [G]Love Thou [C]art
To [C]me, to [G]all Thy [Em]mercies [G]move; Thy [C]nature [Em]and Thy [Dm]name is [G]Love
To [C]me, to [G]all Thy [Em]mercies [G]move; Thy [C]nature [Dm]and Thy [G]name is [C]Love.
{end_of_verse}
